Integrating both sides with respect to $t$, we get
$A(t) e^{t/50} = \int e^{t/50} \left(\frac{1}{2} + \frac{1}{4} \sin t\right) dt = \int \frac{1}{2} e^{t/50} dt + \frac{1}{4} \int e^{t/50} \sin t dt$.
